<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<!--
	Temperatures displayed in the unit of their site: an application-defined primitive type whose
	display depends on the object owning the value.
	
	The minimum and maximum temperature of a sensor are stored in degrees Celsius. The storage of
	the type reads them in the unit of the site the sensor belongs to, so the sensor table and the
	sensor form show them in that unit, and a number typed into the form without a unit is taken in
	that unit as well. A number typed with a unit (20 °C, 68 F, 300 K) is converted.
	
	The sensor table observes the sites as well, so it follows a changed unit of its site at once;
	the sensor form shows the changed unit when it is displayed again.
	
	"New Sensor" creates a sensor in the selected site through a dialog. The sensor being created
	belongs to no site yet, so its temperatures are entered in degrees Celsius unless typed with
	another unit.
-->
<view>
	<channels>
		<channel name="site"/>
		<channel name="sensor"/>
	</channels>

	<panel>
		<title>
			<en>Temperatures</en>
			<de>Temperaturen</de>
		</title>

		<adaptive-detail selection="site">
			<home-label>
				<en>Sites</en>
				<de>Standorte</de>
			</home-label>
			<selector>
				<panel>
					<title>
						<en>Sites</en>
						<de>Standorte</de>
					</title>
					<inset>
						<text>
							<label>
								<en>This demo shows an application-defined value type: the temperatures of the sensors are stored as plain numbers in degrees Celsius, but every display - table, form, label - shows them in the unit of the site the sensor belongs to, and a number typed into a form is read in that unit. Change the unit of a site to see its sensors in another unit. How such a type is built is described in the developer article model/custom-primitive-type.</en>
								<de>Diese Demo zeigt einen anwendungsdefinierten Werttyp: Die Temperaturen der Sensoren werden als einfache Zahlen in Grad Celsius gespeichert, aber jede Anzeige - Tabelle, Formular, Beschriftung - zeigt sie in der Einheit des Standorts, zu dem der Sensor gehört, und eine in ein Formular eingegebene Zahl wird in dieser Einheit gelesen. Ändern Sie die Einheit eines Standorts, um seine Sensoren in einer anderen Einheit zu sehen. Wie ein solcher Typ gebaut wird, beschreibt der Entwicklerartikel model/custom-primitive-type.</de>
							</label>
						</text>
					</inset>
					<table
						observed-types="demo.temperature:DemoSite"
						selection="site"
						types="demo.temperature:DemoSite"
					>
						<columns>
							<column attribute="name"/>
							<column attribute="temperatureUnit"/>
						</columns>
						<rows>all(`demo.temperature:DemoSite`)</rows>
					</table>
				</panel>
			</selector>
			<detail>
				<adaptive-detail
					reset-on="site"
					selection="sensor"
				>
					<selector>
						<panel>
							<title>
								<en>Site</en>
								<de>Standort</de>
							</title>
							<commands>
								<generic-command
									image="css:bi bi-plus-lg"
									inputs="site"
									placement="TOOLBAR"
								>
									<label>
										<en>New Sensor</en>
										<de>Neuer Sensor</de>
									</label>
									<executability>
										<null-input-disabled/>
									</executability>
									<create-transient type="demo.temperature:DemoSensor">
										<with-result>
											<open-dialog
												bind-input-to="model"
												dialog-view="demo/create-sensor.view.xml"
											>
												<bind
													channel="container"
													to="site"
												/>
												<bind
													channel="selection"
													to="sensor"
												/>
											</open-dialog>
										</with-result>
									</create-transient>
								</generic-command>
							</commands>
							<form
								input="site"
								with-inset="true"
							>
								<field attribute="name"/>
								<field attribute="temperatureUnit"/>
							</form>
							<table
								observed-types="demo.temperature:DemoSite,demo.temperature:DemoSensor"
								selection="sensor"
								types="demo.temperature:DemoSensor"
							>
								<columns>
									<column attribute="name"/>
									<column attribute="minTemperature"/>
									<column attribute="maxTemperature"/>
								</columns>
								<inputs>
									<input channel="site"/>
								</inputs>
								<rows>if($site == null, [], $site.get(`demo.temperature:DemoSite#sensors`))</rows>
							</table>
						</panel>
					</selector>
					<detail>
						<panel>
							<title>
								<en>Sensor</en>
								<de>Sensor</de>
							</title>
							<form
								input="sensor"
								with-inset="true"
							>
								<field attribute="name"/>
								<field attribute="minTemperature"/>
								<field attribute="maxTemperature"/>
							</form>
						</panel>
					</detail>
				</adaptive-detail>
			</detail>
		</adaptive-detail>
	</panel>
</view>